// The golden scripts of the window, replayed as cases on the real engine: each is a script in this directory (NAME.txt) and the dump it must end in (NAME.out), here with its text in full because a case cannot name a file. They run on the probability pack (the cases run in the gym directory) with a log of the case's own, the clock fixed at 1760000000000 and the model unreachable, so the hints are the pack's own words. Check them against the files with
//   gym window --pack packs/probability --log LOG --now 1760000000000 --url http://127.0.0.1:1 --script ui/golden/NAME.txt --dump | diff - ui/golden/NAME.out
// (a fresh LOG for full_rep, gate, tap_out, phase and cool; a copy of NAME.log for warmup and score).

// The dump a script ends in: a log of the case's own holding gym_log_text, a session opened on it (planned afresh when the log has none running) and the script replayed.
gym_golden_dump(string gym_script_text, string gym_log_text) {
  string gym_golden_folder = fs_mktemp("gym_golden_", 1);
  int gym_golden_wrote = fs_append_text(gym_golden_folder + "/learner.log", gym_log_text);
  gym_world_open("packs/probability", gym_golden_folder + "/learner.log", 1760000000000, "http://127.0.0.1:1", 1);
} chain (string gym_script_text, string gym_log_text) {
  Session gym_golden_opening = gym_start(0);
  Session[] gym_golden_holder = [gym_golden_opening];
  gym_begin_session((import gym_setting), gym_golden_holder);
} chain (string gym_script_text, string gym_log_text) {
  int gym_golden_bad = gym_replay((import gym_setting), gym_golden_holder, gym_script_text);
  string gym_golden_text = gym_dump(gym_golden_holder[0]);
} return string gym_golden_text;
("# a full rep: type, confidence, submit, hint, hint\ntype 1/3\nconfidence 90\nsubmit\nhint\nhint\n", ""):("screen rep\nclock 0s, Main set, 780s left\nitem 1 of 3, confidence 90, stage committed\ncorrect 1, hints 2, definition none\nanswer 1/3\nnote \nprompt A fair six-sided die is rolled once. What is the probability of rolling a number greater than 4? Give a fraction.\nreference 1/3\nrubric Lists or counts the six equally likely outcomes.; Counts the outcomes greater than 4 and divides by the total.\nrung 1: Begin by writing down every outcome one roll can have.\nrung 2: Which of those outcomes count as \"greater than 4\", and how many outcomes are there altogether?\nRetention: not enough data (n = 0, need 5)\nTransfer: not enough data (n = 0, need 5)\nCalibration: not enough data (n = 1, need 5)\nIndependence: not enough data (n = 1, need 5)\nFluency: not enough data (n = 1, need 5)\ntable 50%: no reps yet\ntable 70%: no reps yet\ntable 90%: 1 rep, 100% right\ntable 99%: no reps yet\nhead from 1 logged attempts")
